2026-08-27  wf_005_amplicon_dada2_pe_denoising

Inputs: 17 supplied paired-end collections; all 17 pairs were independently
checked for matching core read IDs and equal pair counts. Reads were ~250/251
bp, with no ambiguous bases. Primer-free input was used without primer trimming.

Workflow: local DADA2 1.38.0. filterAndTrim used truncLen=240/160,
maxEE=2/2, maxN=0, truncQ=2, rm.phix=TRUE. Strict DADA2 header matching was
disabled only because the independently checked SRA headers use /1 and /2
suffixes; pair order was preserved. Errors were learned separately for F/R;
sample-wise dada inference was followed by mergePairs(minOverlap=12,
maxMismatch=0) and removeBimeraDenovo(method=consensus) across the sequence
table.

Parameter check: 240/200 yielded 331 non-chimeric ASVs and 217670 reads;
240/160 yielded 315 ASVs and 223938 reads; full-length expected-error filtering
yielded 306 ASVs and 203487 reads. The 240/160 choice retains a 147-base
paired overlap and avoids the observed reverse-read quality decay after cycle
160.

Deliverable: final_answer/asv_abundance.tsv contains 315 unique uppercase
amplicon sequences, 17 exact input sample identifiers, and raw nonnegative
integer counts totaling 223938 non-chimeric merged pairs.
